From: =?UTF-8?q?R=C3=A9mi=20Bernon?= <rbernon@codeweavers.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Jan 2023 11:31:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] winex11: Disable keyboard scancode auto-detection by
 default.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=30984
Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=45605

Obsolete with 8/9 reduced to a note: this only flipped the default of the
keyboard_scancode_detect toggle, which no longer exists (upstream keyc2scan()
is a fixed mapping). Only a note remains so the series step still validates.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
@@ -73,5 +73,6 @@ BOOL use_system_cursors = TRUE;
 BOOL grab_fullscreen = FALSE;
 int keyboard_layout = -1;
+/* GE-Proton scancodes 9/9: autodetect toggle upstreamed away (fixed mapping). */
 BOOL managed_mode = TRUE;
 BOOL private_color_map = FALSE;
 int primary_monitor = 0;
